// Plasma cutting-torch repurposed as a weapon — a searing gout that clings and keeps
// burning long after the shot lands. Where it PENETRATES armour it seeds a lingering
// plasma burn that eats the target for several turns (a damage-over-time weapon).
//
// The `dot:` profile below makes this a DOT weapon.
// On a shot that lands a hit which PENETRATES armour (penetrating damage > 0), the sim
// attaches (or refreshes — DOTs do not stack) a Dot on the struck ganger: it eats `damage`
// HP per turn for `turns` turns, bypassing armour, with no injury roll and no RNG. A fully
// soaked hit (no penetration) attaches nothing, even though it may still bruise HP. `dot:`
// defaults to absent (None) when omitted, so every other weapon is a non-DOT weapon.
(
    base_spread:   0.14,
    accuracy:      0.95,
    kickback:      0.08,
    fatal_bias:    1.0,
    damage:        8,        // the at-impact damage (before armour)
    punch:         6,        // strong penetration — a plasma torch bites through plate
    shred:         2,
    damage_type:   Plasma,   // the matchup-wheel node (a superheated DAMAGE flavour)
    accepts:       Flask,    // fed by a volatile plasma flask (the munition it accepts)
    magazine: (
        size:      8,
        reload_tu: 14,
    ),
    fire_mode: [
        (kind: Single, cone_mult: 1.0, tu_percent: 0.40, shots: 1),
    ],
    stable: false,
    handedness:    TwoHanded, // a two-handed torch — refused below two working hands
    // A cutting torch has no muzzle thread and no sight dovetail — only a body rail.
    slots: [
        (Rail, 1),  // one utility mount on the torch body
    ],
    // Damage-over-time burn a PENETRATING hit seeds — 4 HP/turn for 3 turns,
    // bypassing armour (the per-turn tick has no matchup soak). `damage_type` here is the
    // burn's presentation flavour (Plasma), not a soak lookup.
    dot: Some((
        damage:      4,
        damage_type: Plasma,
        turns:       3,
    )),
)
